**A5 wording gap that no check can catch:** A5 says "A whole map is produced only when the user asks for a module map." The *tool* has no notion of "the user asked"; it only sees the command `map`. The evaluator can only check that non-`map` commands don't dump. Whether the agent invokes `map` unasked is agent behavior (P6) — explicitly NOT CHECKED. So A5's third clause is unverifiable by any tool check; a check can only cover the first two clauses. Propose wording: make the tool-side obligation explicit and move the agent-side to the agent's requirement, or phrase it as "No command other than `map` returns map content; the agent asks the user before running `map`." That is a wording proposal.

