- Also "a function reached twice is shown twice" is clear.
- "a link lacks its kind or location" is clear.
- A2's requirement body says "A function reached twice is shown once, with a reference back." Good.

But careful: the brief says "a change to a requirement's wording is a proposal for them, never made by the checks." So I propose wording, don't apply.

Also "say whether a requirement's own wording (A5 or A2) lets a failure pass that no check can catch; if so, propose the wording."

For A5: yes — "A whole map is produced only when the user asks for a module map" cannot be caught by any tool check (agent behavior; P6 marks NOT CHECKED). And "without its limits" is catchable only if "limit that applies" is defined; as worded, a boilerplate limit passes every tool check. That's a wording hole no check can close because the case format checks presence only; and even a stronger check needs the wording to say a limit must be the one reached.

For A2: yes — "an ambiguous match is treated as certain, or a candidate not built is not named" is agent behavior, marked NOT CHECKED; no check catches it. Proposed split.

Also A2: "A known link within the depth is missing" — "known" is by whom? If the check-writer doesn't know the link, no check catches it. The private set supplies "known" links. Wording: "a link that the type checker establishes". Hmm, but A2 is about type-following; R2 covers type. A2's "known link" should be "a link established by the type checker." Propose that to remove the epistemic "known".

